iption:** Measures the proportion of male patients admitted to the hospital versus those followed up at the outpatient clinic.\n\n- **Percentage of Female Patients Born After 1930:**\n  - **Formula:** \\(\\text{Percentage} = \\frac{\\text{COUNT}(\\text{ID}) \\text{ where year(Birthday)} > 1930 \\text{ and SEX} = 'F'}{\\text{COUNT}(\\text{ID}) \\text{ where SEX} = 'F'} \\times 100\\)\n  - **Description:** Calculates the percentage of female patients born after 1930.\n\n- **SLE Diagnosis Inpatient to Outpatient Ratio:**\n  - **Formula:** \\(\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{COUNT}(\\text{ID}) \\text{ where Diagnosis} = 'SLE' \\text{ and Admission} = '+'}{\\text{COUNT}(\\text{ID}) \\text{ where Diagnosis} = 'SLE' \\text{ and Admission} = '-'}\\)\n  - **Description:** Compares the number of inpatients to outpatients among patients diagnosed with SLE.\n\n## 4. Constraints & Conventions\n\n### Filtering Criteria\n- **Gender-Based Filters:** Use 'SEX' field with 'M' for males and 'F' for females.\n- **Admission Status:** Use 'Admission' field with '+' for inpatients and '-' for outpatients.\n\n### Temporal Boundaries\n- **Date Formats:** All dates are stored in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format.\n- **Fiscal Year:** Aligns with the calendar year, starting on January 1st and ending on December 31st.\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- **Age Calculation:** Age is calculated as the difference between the current year and the year of birth.\n\n## 5. Exemplar Use Cases\n\n### Use Case 1: Calculate the Percentage of Male Patients with Abnormal Uric Acid Levels\n- **SQL:** \n  ```sql\n  SELECT CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN UA > 8.0 AND SEX = 'M' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS REAL) * 100 / COUNT(*) FROM Laboratory\n  ```\n- **Explanation:** This query calculates the percentage of male patients with uric acid levels above 8.0.\n\n### Use Case 2: Identify Patients with Severe Thrombosis\n- **SQL:** \n  ```sql\n  SELECT DISTINCT ID, SEX, Diagnosis FROM Examination WHERE Thrombosis = 2\n  ```\n- **Explanation:** Lists patients with a thrombosis level of 2, indicating severe cases.\n\n### Use Case 3: Determine the Average Age of Patients\n- **SQL:** \n  ```",
